      "writtenOn": "2022-12-02T02:05:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Are we getting a protocol error because conflict with the incoming Get_Status message? (I would have thought that collision avoidance would take care of this too.)\n\nI suspect this is it, the second Alert collides with Get_Status/Status from the first Alert. I setup an EC image with a console command that sent 2 Alerts 30 ms apart to test this. When connected to a PD 3.1 Dock which responds to Alert with Get_Status, I was able to reproduce the issue. When connected to a PD 3.1 charger which responds to Alert with Not_Supported, there was no issue.\n\n\u003e Is that what happens now?\n\nNo, it looks like with this soft reset we end up hard resetting and the second Alert gets lost. (https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hdiOwnF0Lo500Mppg02eoTy1P3vIt9mR/view?usp\u003dsharing). I\u0027ll take a closer look at how to avoid this and attempt to resend the Alert, then followup with a patchset.\n\n\u003e That would make sense if we\u0027re the sink and the partner is in control of collision avoidance, and the partner had an immediate response to our alert.\n\nWe are the sink and the partner does immediately respond to the Alert. I attached a trace to the bug, they respond in about 23ms.",
      "parentUuid": "6ef948b5_ec73d9af",
      "revId": "23a2c3afc4c2eea24a12bbf6cc77f6e89e72fd88",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
